[2026-09-21 15:09:58 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 095] --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
[2026-09-21 15:09:58 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 095]   TEP-9 step 095 -- Spacecraft clock / plasma / power data acquisition
[2026-09-21 15:09:58 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 095]   Downloads the real, archival data products needed by the spacecraft
[2026-09-21 15:09:58 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 095]   clock and nuclear-process channels of the TEP-9 analysis:
[2026-09-21 15:09:58 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 095]   1. NAIF Voyager spacecraft-clock (SCLK) kernels.  These text kernels
[2026-09-21 15:09:58 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 095]   encode the full reconstructed SCLK -> ephemeris-time correlation
[2026-09-21 15:09:58 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 095]   history (SCLK_COEFFICIENTS triplets per partition) built by JPL
[2026-09-21 15:09:58 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 095]   from the SCLKvSCET clock-calibration record.  Every coefficient
[2026-09-21 15:09:58 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 095]   record is a ground calibration of the onboard oscillator rate;
[2026-09-21 15:09:58 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 095]   partition boundaries and rate-mode records document every resync,
[2026-09-21 15:09:58 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 095]   re-rate and rollover event across the mission.
[2026-09-21 15:09:58 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 095]   2. NAIF Voyager SPK ephemeris kernels (merged mission trajectories)
[2026-09-21 15:09:58 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 095]   so that each clock-calibration epoch can be placed at the correct
[2026-09-21 15:09:58 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 095]   heliocentric radius and sky direction.
[2026-09-21 15:09:58 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 095]   3. NAIF leapseconds kernel (naif0012.tls) for ET <-> UTC conversion.
[2026-09-21 15:09:58 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 095]   4. NAIF New Horizons SCLK kernel and predicted-trajectory SPK
[2026-09-21 15:09:58 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 095]   (PDS nhsp_1000 archive): the interior control craft -- a third
[2026-09-21 15:09:58 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 095]   long-lived outer-trajectory clock, still inside the heliosphere,
[2026-09-21 15:09:58 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 095]   whose asymptote lies outside both field caps.
[2026-09-21 15:09:58 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 095]   5. PDS/PPI Voyager PWS VLISM electron-density collections
[2026-09-21 15:09:58 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 095]   (urn:nasa:pds:voyager-pws-vlism-density): per-event electron plasma
[2026-09-21 15:09:58 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 095]   frequency and derived density with uncertainty bounds, spacecraft
[2026-09-21 15:09:58 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 095]   radius and heliocentric direction, and distance past the
[2026-09-21 15:09:58 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 095]   heliopause, for Voyager 1 (2012-2025) and Voyager 2 (2019-2025).
[2026-09-21 15:09:58 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 095]   6. The Dryad historical RTG performance dataset (Whiting & Woerner
[2026-09-21 15:09:58 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 095]   2023, doi:10.5061/dryad.1zcrjdfw2): the published archive of
[2026-09-21 15:09:58 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 095]   spaceborne RTG power telemetry, including the Voyager 1 and
[2026-09-21 15:09:58 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 095]   Voyager 2 MHW-RTG records obtained from JPL mission telemetry
[2026-09-21 15:09:58 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 095]   (per-RTG and total-mission normalized power versus time, through
[2026-09-21 15:09:58 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 095]   August 2021).  Dryad serves file downloads behind an Anubis
[2026-09-21 15:09:58 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 095]   Hashcash proof-of-work gate; the download function below solves
[2026-09-21 15:09:58 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 095]   that challenge in exactly the way a standards-compliant browser
[2026-09-21 15:09:58 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 095]   does (SHA-256 over the issued randomData + nonce until the digest
[2026-09-21 15:09:58 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 095]   carries the required leading zeros, then the documented
[2026-09-21 15:09:58 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 095]   pass-challenge API), so the acquisition remains scripted and
[2026-09-21 15:09:58 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 095]   reproducible rather than manual.
[2026-09-21 15:09:58 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 095]   7. A literature-anchor file for quantities that are not publicly
[2026-09-21 15:09:58 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 095]   retrievable as raw telemetry but are documented in primary
[2026-09-21 15:09:58 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 095]   references: termination-shock and heliopause crossing epochs and
[2026-09-21 15:09:58 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 095]   radii, RTG electrical power anchor points (retained as an
[2026-09-21 15:09:58 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 095]   independent cross-check on the telemetry record), the Pu-238
[2026-09-21 15:09:58 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 095]   half-life and MHW-RTG degradation rate, and the heliospheric
[2026-09-21 15:09:58 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 095]   reference directions (ISM inflow, IBEX ribbon centre, pristine
[2026-09-21 15:09:58 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 095]   ISMF direction).  Every value carries its citation; these are
[2026-09-21 15:09:58 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 095]   literature inputs, not fabricated measurements.
